From: Yury Ilyanok <yury.ilyanok@gmail.com>
Subject: net: phy: realtek: support a fixed 2500BASE-X host on RTL8221B

When an RTL8221B faces a host SerDes that is hard-fixed at 2500BASE-X
and cannot dynamically change interface mode (e.g. the RTL9303 switch
ports on the Verizon CR1000A), two parts of rtl822xb_config_init()
break the data path:

 - the rate-adapter register block (VEND1 0x75f3/0x6a04/0x6f10/0x6f11
   plus PHYCR1) programmed by the gen1=false path stops client frames
   from ever reaching the host MAC (in_octets frozen), even for a
   native 2.5G client needing no rate adaptation;

 - for a sub-2.5G client the PHY drops its system side to SGMII
   (1.25 Gbaud).  The fixed host SerDes cannot follow, so the port
   links but never forwards.

On boards that declare the constraint with a new
"realtek,host-2500base-x-fixed" PHY node property, use the gen1 path
(SerDes option still selected, magic block skipped) and pin the system
side to a constant 2500BASE-X line via the vendor SerDes-mode registers
(VEND2 0xD032=0x24, 0xD034=0x03) so sub-rate clients are rate-adapted
inside the PHY (PAUSE) instead of by switching the line rate.  PHYs
without the property are unaffected.

Signed-off-by: Yury Ilyanok <yury.ilyanok@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c
@@ -1444,7 +1444,39 @@
 
 static int rtl822xb_config_init(struct phy_device *phydev)
 {
-	return rtl822x_set_serdes_option_mode(phydev, false);
+	int ret;
+
+	if (!of_property_read_bool(phydev->mdio.dev.of_node,
+				   "realtek,host-2500base-x-fixed"))
+		return rtl822x_set_serdes_option_mode(phydev, false);
+
+	/* The host SerDes this PHY faces is fixed at 2500BASE-X and does not
+	 * participate in the PHY's rate-adapter handshake.  Take the gen1
+	 * path: the 2500BASE-X SerDes option is still selected (link comes
+	 * up) but the rate-adapter register block is skipped -- with it
+	 * written, client frames never reach the host MAC.
+	 */
+	ret = rtl822x_set_serdes_option_mode(phydev, true);
+	if (ret < 0)
+		return ret;
+
+	/* Keep the system side at a constant 2500BASE-X line.  Left to its
+	 * dynamic default the PHY drops to SGMII for a sub-2.5G client, which
+	 * a fixed-2500BASE-X host SerDes cannot follow (port links but never
+	 * forwards).  Sub-rate clients are rate-adapted inside the PHY
+	 * instead.
+	 */
+	ret = phy_modify_mmd(phydev, MDIO_MMD_VEND1, RTL822X_VND1_SERDES_OPTION,
+			     RTL822X_VND1_SERDES_OPTION_MODE_MASK,
+			     RTL822X_VND1_SERDES_OPTION_MODE_2500BASEX);
+	if (ret < 0)
+		return ret;
+
+	ret = phy_write_mmd(phydev, MDIO_MMD_VEND2, 0xd032, 0x0024);
+	if (ret < 0)
+		return ret;
+
+	return phy_write_mmd(phydev, MDIO_MMD_VEND2, 0xd034, 0x0003);
 }
 
 static int rtl822x_serdes_write(struct phy_device *phydev, u16 reg, u16 val)
